.TH SXAC 1 sxac\-VERSION
.SH NAME
sxac \- simple X auto clicker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sxac
.RB [ \-b
.IR button ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR delay ]
.RB [ \-h ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sxac
clicks a mouse button wherever the pointer is, at a fixed interval, through the XTest extension of the X server named by
.BR DISPLAY .
It clicks until it receives SIGINT or SIGTERM.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-b " button"
Click button 1 (left), 2 (middle) or 3 (right). The default is 1.
.TP
.BI \-d " delay"
Wait
.I delay
milliseconds between clicks. The default is 100.
.TP
.B \-h
Print usage and exit.
.SH NOTES
A short delay can make the desktop hard to use while sxac runs. Ctrl+C stops it in the foreground of a terminal, and
.B pkill sxac
stops it from anywhere else.
